# Mosquitto ACL notes:
# - `topic` lines BEFORE any `user` directive apply to anonymous clients only.
# - `pattern` lines apply to EVERY username (including future gw0001 / gw0010 / …).
#   New gateways therefore do not need a new ACL block for GwData / SrvData / GwStatus.
# - Authenticated users still need CONNECT rights (password_file / allow_anonymous).

# Shared device/platform topics for all clients
pattern readwrite GwData
pattern readwrite SrvData
pattern readwrite GwStatus
pattern write _health/%u
pattern readwrite sandbox/%u/#

# Anonymous (only used when allow_anonymous is true)
topic readwrite GwData
topic readwrite SrvData
topic readwrite GwStatus

# Gateway / platform shared account
user user
topic readwrite GwData
topic readwrite SrvData
topic readwrite GwStatus

# Platform MQTT worker (must match infra MQTT_USERNAME)
user asset_platform_local
topic readwrite GwData
topic readwrite SrvData
topic readwrite GwStatus
